{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting you shall sit day and night seven days.</b> He warned them not to leave the entrance of the Tent of Meeting day and night during the time of the service, that is, until they complete all the service incumbent upon them at that time. And this is a commandment applying to all generations, that a priest may not leave the service and go out — and this is what is said concerning the High Priest (Leviticus 21): ״ומן המקדש לא יצא ולא יחלל״ — 'and from the Sanctuary he shall not go out and he shall not profane.' When is it that he may not go out and may not profane? You should say: during the time of the service. And if he did so, he is liable to death, as it is stated: ״פן תמותו״ — 'lest you die'; and from the negative you infer the positive." "<b>And what</b> he warned them, that they should not leave the entrance, neither by day nor by night — the intent of the verse concerns the hours suited to sit there, for he is flesh and blood, compelled to attend to his physical needs. Similarly, Scripture said concerning the building of the Temple (I Kings 6:38): ״ויבנהו שבע שנים״ — 'and he built it seven years,' and (ibid. 7:1): ״ואת ביתו בנה שלמה שלש עשרה שנה״ — 'and his own house Solomon built thirteen years' — the Sabbaths and festivals are not to be included in them, for the intent is the days suited for labor. So too here, he warned them not to leave the entrance during the hours suited to sit there." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״ופתח אהל מועד תשבו יומם ולילה״ — these are the seven days of mourning for Nadav and Avihu, for the Holy One, blessed be He, watched over His world first. The explanation: He mourned seven days over the world that was destined to be destroyed in the generation of the Flood, as it is stated (Genesis 7): ״ויהי לשבעת הימים ומי המבול היו על הארץ״. And they said there: one does not mourn for the dead before he dies; rather, a person who does not know what will be does not mourn until the dead person dies — but the Holy One, blessed be He, who knows what will be, watched over His world first. So too here, the Holy One, blessed be He, said: ״ופתח אהל מועד תשבו יומם ולילה שבעת ימים״ — watch over your brothers for seven days, just as I watched over My world for seven. And this is what is written: ״ושמרתם את משמרת ה׳״ — 'and you shall keep the watch of HaShem.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:11.547596917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}